  "description_short": "Roadside coffee stop at Storms River serving Mugg & Bean favourites before exploring Tsitsikamma.",
  "description_long": "Conveniently located at the TotalEnergies Petroport along the N2, Mugg & Bean On The Move offers a reliable pit stop for travellers passing through Storms River. It's the kind of place where you grab a decent cappuccino and a toasted sandwich before heading into Tsitsikamma's forests or continuing your Garden Route journey.\n\nThe menu covers the familiar Mugg & Bean range — generous burgers, all-day breakfast options, and their signature oversized muffins. Service is geared for efficiency, making it practical for a quick break rather than a leisurely meal. The setting is functional roadside rather than scenic, but when you need fuel and caffeine between destinations, it does the job without fuss.\n\nIt's particularly handy if you're travelling with family or need takeaway options for the road. While it won't be your most memorable Garden Route dining experience, it serves its purpose as a convenient refreshment stop in an area where options are limited.",
